Graph Traversal using DFS and BFS

Aim:
To implement Graph Traversal using DFS and BFS in Python.

Description:

DFS (Depth First Search): Visits a node and goes as deep as possible before backtracking.
BFS (Breadth First Search): Visits nodes level by level.
The graph is represented using a dictionary (adjacency list).

Output:

DFS: 0 1 3 2 4
BFS: 0 1 2 3 4
Time Complexity: O(V + E)

Conclusion:
DFS and BFS graph traversal are successfully implemented using Python.
Both algorithms visit all connected vertices of the graph.